{
 "note": "THREE-WAY endpoint reconciliation: IP2025 MINDEF.PAR vs Techlog QM_MineralTable vs SandiMin multimin_ref_spec sec-I. Common unit basis: RHOB g/cc, NPHI fraction(v/v), DT us/ft, U(=PEF*rhoe) barns/cc, SIGMA c.u., GR API, CEC meq/g. Conversions applied: SandiMin RHOB kg/m3 /1000, SandiMin DT us/m /3.2808. IP unit conventions: Density g/cc(native), Sonic us/ft(native), Neutron fraction(native), U barns/cc(native), SIGMA c.u.(native). KEY IP CONVENTION: IP MINDEF.PAR has NO direct GR endpoint column - GR is computed at runtime from K_Conc/Th_Conc/U_Conc weight-fraction columns, so GR is reported as a 2-way Techlog-vs-SandiMin check only. IP CEC: MINDEF stores Qv in meq/cm3 of WET clay; converted to meq/g via CEC=Qv/(GrainDensity_dry*(1-PhiTClay)). Clay density: IP Density col is IP's own wet-clay-model endpoint, whereas Techlog/SandiMin use dry-clay density - clay RHOB divergence is a model-convention difference, not an error. Mineral name alignment via ElanToIPMapping.par (QUAR/DOLO/CALC/ILLI/KAOL/CHLO/ALBI/MONT/etc).",
